{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{artist: Thomas Chisholm and Music by William M. Runyan}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Great is thy [G]faithfulness, [A]O God my [D]Father,
[G]There is no [D]shadow of [E]turning with [A]Thee;
[A7]Thou changest [D]not, Thy compassions they [G6]fail not
[E/G#]As Thou has [D/A]been, Thou [A]forever wilt [D]be.

{comment: Chorus}
[A]Great is Thy [D]faithfulness!
[B]Great is Thy [Em]faithfulness!
[A]Morning by [D]morning new [E]mercies I [A]see.
[A]All I have [D]needed Thy hand hath [G6]provided
[E/G#]Great is Thy [D/A]faithfulness, [A]Lord unto [D]me.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Summer and [G]winter, and [A]springtime and [D]harvest,
[G]Sun, moon, and [D]stars in their [E]courses [A]above
[A7]Join with all [D]nature in manifold [G6]witness
[E/G#]To Thy great [D/A]faithfulness, [A]mercy and [D]love.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Pardon for [G]sin and a [A]peace that [D]endureth,
[G]Thy own dear [D]presence to [E]cheer and to [A]guide.
[A7]Strength for [D]today and bright hope for [G6]tomorrow
[E/G#]Blessings all [D/A]mine, with ten [A]thousand [D]beside.
